To take the difference, the $\ln$ has the nice property of being symmetric and the dollar difference would not matter, there is a scale invariance. However, we lose some of the firms that have a negative implied value. This could introduce some bias for positive firms. The solution right now is to look at the difference using full implied EV and not only equity. With this, we can recover quite a few firms. And the ones that we cannot recover are most likely.


